  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* VacSweep[S,P,sub]: for each of the six vacuum weights, solve and compare against the\n   independently-predicted τvacP. Columns:\n     #sol       must be 1 (weight multiplicity 1)\n     bad coeff  Baxter residual coefficients that are not exactly 0, over all four branches\n     τ mismatch coefficients of τ_1,τ_2,τ_3 differing from the τvacP prediction\n   Both must be 0. Everything here is rational, so these are exact statements. *)\nClearAll[VacSweep];\nVacSweep[S_, P_, sub_: {}] := Module[{x},\n  Prepend[\n   Table[Module[{l1, l2, ord, t, recs, r, mism},\n     {l1, l2} = siteWeights[S, P, n]; ord = vacOrder[S, P, n];\n     {t, recs} = AbsoluteTiming[TwistedSolve[S, P, n, sub]];\n     If[recs === {} || recs === $Failed, {n, Mdeg[S, P, n], 0, \"-\", \"-\", Round[t, 0.001]},\n      r = First[recs];\n      mism = Count[\n        Flatten@Table[\n          CoefficientList[Expand[Together[(τ[a][S, P, n][x] /. Thread[tcvars -> r[\"tc\"]]) - τvacP[l1, l2, ord][a][x] /. sub]], x],\n          {a, 3}], c_ /; Simplify[c] =!= 0];\n      {n, Mdeg[S, P, n], Length[recs], verifyTwisted[S, P, n, r, sub], mism, Round[t, 0.001]}]],\n    {n, vacWeights[S, P]}],\n   {\"weight n\", \"M_k\", \"#sol\", \"bad coeff\", \"τ mismatch\", \"t/s\"}]];\n\nGrid[VacSweep[1, 1, num], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
