"></span></span><span style=\"top:-20.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:13.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-21.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:13.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-22.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:13.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-24.1em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:13.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-25.3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:13.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:11.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[80]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{(S,P)} & \\text{weight n} & \\text{W\\_1234 - V A(u)A(u-h)}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{2,2,0,0\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{2,0,2,0\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{2,0,0,2\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{0,2,2,0\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{0,2,0,2\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{0,0,2,2\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{3,3,0,0\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{3,0,3,0\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{3,0,0,3\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{0,3,3,0\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{0,3,0,3\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{0,0,3,3\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{4,4,0,0\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{4,0,4,0\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{4,0,0,4\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{0,4,4,0\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{0,4,0,4\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{0,0,4,4\\right\\} & 0\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "c95bd32d-a220-4c38-beea-d40cb20faa16"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Behaviour as the twist is switched off\n\nParametrise `z_j = 1 + eps psi_j`. This is rational in `eps`, so `TwistedSolve` can be run with `eps`\nfully symbolic and the results expanded exactly — no numerics, no state-tracking.\n\nThe untwisted equation has polynomial solutions of the *staggered* degrees `Mhat_k = M_k + (k-1)`\n(`degQ` of `baxter_SU4_L2_XXX.wb`). A monic `q_k` of degree `M_k` must therefore tend to an\nuntwisted solution of degree at most `M_k`, and for `k >= 2` the only one available is the branch-1\nsolution, of degree `M_1 < M_k`. Monic normalisation then forces a blow-up:\n\n$$ [u^j]\\,q_k = O\\big(\\varepsilon^{-(M_k-\\max(j,M_1))}\\big),\\qquad q_k=O\\big(\\varepsilon^{-(M_k-M_1)}\\big).$$\n\nIn the wedge those divergences cancel, because the limit of `q_k` is *proportional to* the limit of\n`q_1`. What survives is one power of `eps` per pair of colliding twists — exactly `V_I`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* eps-parametrisation and an exact leading-order extractor. *)\nClearAll[ordE];\npsi = {1, 1/3, 1/5, 1/7};\nepsSub[SS_, PP_] := Join[{θ1 -> 1/3, θ2 -> 1/7, h -> 1}, Table[z[j] -> 1 + eps psi[[j]], {j, 4}]];\neps1 = epsSub[1, 1];\nordE[e_] := Module[{s = Series[Together[Simplify[e]], {eps, 0, 12}]},\n   Which[PossibleZeroQ[Normal[s]], Infinity, Head[s] === SeriesData, s[[4]]/s[[6]], True, 0]];\n\n(* Degrees admitted by the UNTWISTED equation, by direct monic solvability. This both confirms\n   Mhat_k = M_k + (k-1) and identifies which solution of a degenerate weight sector is the state\n   that becomes highest weight. NB: counting nullspace dimensions instead silently misses a jump\n   when two admissible degrees are adjacent — test monic solvability, not rank. *)\nClearAll[degMonic];\ndegMonic[SS_, PP_, μ_, tc0_, dmax_] := Module[{x, unt, out = {}},\n   unt[qf_] := Expand[Together[BaxRes[SS, PP, μ][1][qf][x] /. Thread[tcvars -> tc0]\n       /. {θ1 -> 1/3, θ2 -> 1/7, h -> 1} /. Table[z[j] -> 1, {j, 4}]]];\n   Do[If[Quiet@Solve[Thread[CoefficientList[unt[Function[y, y^d + Sum[cq[j] y^j, {j, 0, d - 1}]]], x] == 0],\n         Table[cq[j], {j, 0, d - 1}]] =!= {}, AppendTo[out, d]], {d, 0, dmax}];\n   out];",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Report: for a given solution record, the eps-orders of the coefficients of each monic q_k and\n   of each q_I = W_I/V_I. Regular = every order >= 0. *)\nClearAll[ordReport];\nordReport[rec_, sub_, sets_] := Module[{x},\n  Prepend[Join[\n    Table[{{k}, \"q_\" <> ToString[k], rec[\"M\"][[k]], ordE /@ (rec[\"q\"][[k]] /. sub)}, {k, 4}],\n    Table[{II, \"q_I = W_I/V_I\", Total[rec[\"M\"][[II]]],\n           ordE /@ CoefficientList[Collect[Cancel[Together[qWronsk[rec, II][x] /. sub]], x], x]}, {II, sets}]],\n   {\"I\", \"object\", \"degree\", \"eps orders of coefficients\"}]];\n\n(* State A: (S,P)=(1,1), weight {2,1,1,0}. Two solutions; the one that becomes highest weight is\n   picked out by its untwisted degree spectrum {0,2,3,5} = M + (k-1). M = {0,1,1,2}. *)\nModule[{sols, sel},\n  sols = TwistedSolve[1, 1, {2, 1, 1, 0}, eps1];\n  sel = Select[sols, degMonic[1, 1, {2, 1, 1, 0}, Simplify[Limit[#[\"tc\"], eps -> 0]], 6] === Mdeg[1, 1, {2, 1, 1, 0}] + Range[0, 3] &];\n  stateA = First[sel];\n  Grid[ordReport[stateA, eps1, {{1, 2}, {1, 3}, {2, 3}, {1, 2, 3}, {1, 2, 4}, {2, 3, 4}, {1, 2, 3, 4}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"516305\" data-output-id=\"29\" data-out-n=\"90\" data-sub-idx=\"4\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"28\" data-sub-start=\"12\" data-sub-end=\"16\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[90]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"19\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:14.44em;vertical-align:-6.95em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:7.49em;\"><span style=\"top:-9.45em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.45em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:14.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-6.95em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:7.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-9.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">I</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-8.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.21em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=