  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* State B: the LOWEST-weight vacuum n = {0,0,S+P,S+P}, M = {S+P,S+P,0,0}. Multiplicity 1 and\n   rational, so this is cheap and exact. The flag is reversed here: the divergence sits in q_1,q_2\n   and the regular chain is {3,4} in {2,3,4} in {1,2,3,4}. Same rule (lower sets of M), roles\n   permuted — which is the point of including it. *)\nModule[{r = First[TwistedSolve[1, 1, {0, 0, 2, 2}, eps1]]},\n  Grid[ordReport[r, eps1, {{3, 4}, {1, 2}, {1, 4}, {2, 3, 4}, {1, 3, 4}, {1, 2, 3}, {1, 2, 3, 4}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
