  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* State D: (S,P)=(3,1), μ={3,3,1,1}, M={1,1,3,3}. The case that exercises BOTH M_1>0 (so q_1 is a\n   genuine polynomial, not a constant) AND M_k>M_1 (so branches 3,4 really do diverge) on a true\n   highest-weight state. Weight multiplicity 7, so the symbolic-eps solve is algebraic of degree 7;\n   instead solve the UNTWISTED problem exactly (staggered degrees Mhat = M+(k-1) = {1,2,5,6}, with\n   the usual gauge fixing), then at each small rational eps pick the branch converging to that tc0.\n   The selection is validated by dist(tc,tc0) ~ eps. *)\nClearAll[UntwSolve];\nUntwSolve[SS_, PP_, μ_, sub_] := Module[{Ms, Mh, x, eqs = {}, unk, gauge = {}, sol, R, z1 = Table[z[j] -> 1, {j, 4}]},\n   Ms = Mdeg[SS, PP, μ]; Mh = Ms + Range[0, 3];\n   Do[R = Expand[Together[(BaxRes[SS, PP, μ][k][qmonic[k, Mh[[k]]]][x] /. z1) /. sub]];\n      eqs = Join[eqs, DeleteCases[CoefficientList[R, x], 0]];\n      gauge = Join[gauge, Table[qc[k, Mh[[j]]], {j, k - 1}]], {k, 4}];\n   unk = Join[tcvars, Flatten[Table[qc[k, j], {k, 4}, {j, 0, Mh[[k]] - 1}]]];\n   sol = Solve[Join[Thread[eqs == 0], Thread[gauge == 0]], unk];\n   {Length[sol], tcvars /. First[sol], Mh}];\n\nuntw31 = UntwSolve[3, 1, {3, 3, 1, 1}, {θ1 -> 1/3, θ2 -> 1/7, h -> 1}];\n{\"#untwisted solutions\" -> untw31[[1]], \"tc0\" -> untw31[[2]], \"untwisted degrees\" -> untw31[[3]]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
