   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 7. Vacuum factors, and the divergence of `q_3`, `q_4`\n\nEq. (C6) of the structure-constants paper reads `Q_ij = W(Q_i,Q_j)`, `Q_theta Q_ijk = W(Q_i,Q_j,Q_k)`,\n`Q_1234 = W(Q_1,..,Q_4)`, with `Q_theta(u) = Prod_alpha (u - theta_alpha)` of degree `L`. Here `L` is\nreplaced by `S+P` and `Q_theta` by the same `A` that appeared in the 4-index Casoratian:\n\n$$ A(u)=\\prod_{j=1}^{S}(u-\\theta_1-jh)\\prod_{j=1}^{P}(u-\\theta_2-jh),\\qquad \\deg A = S+P .$$\n\nVerified exactly (`PolynomialRemainder` = 0, quotient monic of the stated degree) on all six vacuum\nweights at `(2,1)` and `(3,1)`, on the pseudovacuum at four `(S,P)`, and on state A:\n\n| `I` | `W_I` | `deg q~_I` |\n|---|---|---|\n| `{1}` | `q_1` | `M_1` |\n| `{1,2}` | `V_12 q~_12` | `M_1+M_2` |\n| `{1,2,3}` | `V_123 A(u) q~_123` | `M_1+M_2+M_3-(S+P)` |\n| `{1,2,3,4}` | `V_1234 A(u)A(u-h)` | `0` |\n\nThese degrees are exactly what the untwisted Casoratians give: at `z=1` the `k x k` Casoratian of\npolynomials of degrees `Mhat_k = M_k+(k-1)` drops by one per pair, `Sum Mhat - k(k-1)/2`, which\nreproduces each row above after removing the `A` factors. So the vacuum-factor count and the\nstaggering are the same statement.\n\n### The uniform count\n\nDivide the `k x k` relation by `V_{1..k-1}`. This strips every divergence and leaves a\n`(k-1)`-th order difference operator `O_k` with **regular** coefficients of degree `Sum_{i<k} M_i`:\n\n$$ O_k[q_k] \\;=\\; \\Big(\\prod_{i<k}(z_i-z_k)\\Big)\\times(\\text{vacuum factor})\\times \\tilde q_{1\\ldots k}. $$\n\nThree facts then fix `p_k`:\n\n1. **Source**: `eps`-order `k-1` (one twist difference per `i<k`), and degree `Sum_{i<=k} M_i`.\n2. **Operator**: at `eps=0`, `O_k` maps degree `d` to degree `Sum_{i<k}M_i + d - (k-1)` — one drop\n   per pair. Its polynomial kernel is exactly the untwisted `span{P_1,..,P_{k-1}}`, of degrees\n   `Mhat_1,..,Mhat_{k-1}` (so the drop is larger at those special `d`, which do not occur below).\n3. **Tower**: writing `q_k = eps^{-p} sum_j eps^j g_j`, one has `g_0 ~ q_1` (degree `M_1`) and\n   `deg g_j = M_1 + j` — one degree bought per order in `eps`, which is the same one-per-confluence\n   -step that produces `Mhat_k = M_k + (k-1)`.\n\nThe source enters at `j = p + k - 1`, so matching degrees:\n\n$$ \\sum_{i<k}M_i + \\big(M_1+p+k-1\\big) - (k-1) \\;=\\; \\sum_{i\\le k}M_i \\;\\Longrightarrow\\;\n \\boxed{\\,p_k = M_k - M_1\\,} $$\n\nuniformly in `k`. For `k=2` this is the first-order/`eps^1` case derived earlier; `k=3` uses the\n`A`-factor above, `k=4` uses `A(u)A(u-h)`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* The vacuum factor A divides W_123/V_123 exactly, with monic quotient of the predicted degree.\n   Rational states only, so this is exact. *)\nModule[{x},\n Grid[Prepend[Flatten[Table[\n    Table[With[{r = First[TwistedSolve[sp[[1]], sp[[2]], n, num]], SS = sp[[1]], PP = sp[[2]]},\n      With[{W = Cancel[Together[Wronsk[r, {1, 2, 3}][x]/Vand[{1, 2, 3}] /. num]], Ax = (AA[sp[[1]], sp[[2]]][x] /. num)},\n       {sp, n, r[\"M\"], Total[r[\"M\"][[{1, 2, 3}]]] - (SS + PP),\n        Simplify[PolynomialRemainder[W, Ax, x]],\n        Exponent[Simplify[PolynomialQuotient[W, Ax, x]], x],\n        Simplify[Coefficient[PolynomialQuotient[W, Ax, x], x, Exponent[Simplify[PolynomialQuotient[W, Ax, x]], x]]]}]],\n     {n, vacWeights[sp[[1]], sp[[2]]]}], {sp, {{2, 1}, {3, 1}}}], 1],\n   {\"(S,P)\", \"weight\", \"M\", \"pred deg q~123\", \"remainder mod A\", \"deg quotient\", \"lead coeff\"}],\n  Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
