  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 8.1 The leading order is already known exactly\n\nThe order-`eps^0` problem is the **untwisted** one, and `Experiments/baxter_SU4_L2_XXX.wb` already solves it in closed form for arbitrary `(S,P)` and arbitrary `mu`: `tau_1, tau_2, tau_3` as explicit functions of the two Casimirs, and the four `q_k` at degrees `degQ[mu,S,P] = (S+P) - mu_k + (k-1)`, which is **exactly our `Mhat`**. Verified there over the full tensor-product decomposition up to `(S,P)=(8,8)`.\n\nSo there is nothing to solve at order 0 and no branching to resolve. Ported here with renamed symbols (suffix `U`) because that notebook keeps `t`, `S`, `P`, `nu_i`, `irreps` as globals and shares kernel K1 with this one.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* --- Untwisted (leading-order) machinery, ported from baxter_SU4_L2_XXX.wb ---\n   Renamed with a U suffix to avoid the global-symbol collisions with that notebook.\n   nu_1 = nu_2 and nu_3 = nu_4 exactly as in Section 1 here. *)\nClearAll[n1U, n3U, nuU, t1U, t2U, t3U, t4U, BaxU, aU, bU, cU, dU];\nn1U[u_] := (u - θ1 - S h) (u - θ2 - P h);\nn3U[u_] := (u - θ1) (u - θ2);\nnuU[1] = n1U; nuU[2] = n1U; nuU[3] = n3U; nuU[4] = n3U;\n\nt1U[u_] := 4 u^2 + aU[1] u + bU[1];\nt2U[u_] := 6 u^4 + aU[2] u^3 + bU[2] u^2 + cU[2] u + dU[2];\nt3U[u_] := n3U[u] (u - θ1 - h (S + 2)) (u - θ2 - h (P + 2)) (4 u^2 - 4 u (θ1 + θ2) + 4 θ1 θ2 - 2 h P u - 2 h S u - 8 h u + bU[3]);\nt4U[u_] := n1U[u - 3 h] n1U[u - 2 h] n3U[u - h] n3U[u];\n\nBaxU[Q_] := Q[u + h] - t1U[u]/n1U[u] Q[u] + t2U[u]/n1U[u]/n1U[u - h] Q[u - h]\n   - t3U[u]/n1U[u]/n1U[u - h]/n1U[u - 2 h] Q[u - 2 h]\n   + t4U[u]/n1U[u]/n1U[u - h]/n1U[u - 2 h]/n1U[u - 3 h] Q[u - 3 h];\n\n(* Asymptotic solve: orders 1/u..1/u^3 pin 5 of the 7 coefficients; only bU[2], dU[2] survive\n   and they ARE the two Casimirs. *)\nasympSolU = First@Solve[Thread[Flatten[Table[CoefficientList[\n     Coefficient[Expand@Normal@Series[BaxU[Q]/Q[u] /. Q[u_] -> u^p /. (u + x_)^y_ -> u^y (1 + x/u)^y, {u, Infinity, 3}], u, -mo], p], {mo, 3}]] == 0],\n   {aU[1], aU[2], bU[1], cU[2], bU[3]}];\nColumn[asympSolU]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
