  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Bridge: the ported closed forms give this notebook's five tc at order eps^0 with NO solving,\n   for arbitrary (S,P) and arbitrary mu. Matching tau_1..tau_3 at z->1 determines tcvars; tau_4\n   must then agree automatically (it is the quantum determinant, central and already known). *)\nClearAll[tc0U, z1sub];\nz1sub = Table[z[j] -> 1, {j, 4}];\ntc0U[μ_, SS_, PP_] := tc0U[μ, SS, PP] = Module[{x, eqs, sol},\n   eqs = Flatten[Table[CoefficientList[Expand[\n        ((τ[a][SS, PP, μ][x] /. z1sub) - {tau1U[μ][x] /. {S -> SS, P -> PP},\n                                          tau2cU[μ, SS, PP][x],\n                                          tau3U[μ][x] /. {S -> SS, P -> PP}}[[a]])], x], {a, 3}]];\n   sol = Solve[Thread[eqs == 0], tcvars];\n   If[sol === {}, $Failed, tcvars /. First[sol]]];\n\n(* Consistency of the port with this notebook's own conventions:\n   (i) the match is solvable at all (overdetermined: 3+5+7 = 15 equations for 5 unknowns),\n   (ii) tau_4 agrees identically,\n   (iii) at the pseudovacuum tc0U reproduces the exact tcExact0 found earlier. *)\nModule[{x, μ = {2, 1, 1, 0}},\n {\"tc0U[{2,1,1,0},1,1]\" -> (tc0U[μ, 1, 1] /. th),\n  \"tau4 agrees\" -> Simplify[(τ[4][1, 1, μ][x] /. z1sub) - (tau4U[x] /. {S -> 1, P -> 1})] === 0,\n  \"pseudovacuum: tc0U - tcExact0\" -> Simplify[(tc0U[{2, 2, 0, 0}, 1, 1] /. th) - tcExact0],\n  \"pseudovacuum: tc0U - order-0 solve\" -> Simplify[(tc0U[{2, 2, 0, 0}, 1, 1] /. th) - (Table[pv[tc[i], 0], {i, 5}] /. First[sol0])]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
