  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* State D: (S,P)=(3,1), mu={3,3,1,1}, M={1,1,3,3}, Mhat={1,2,5,6}. Unlike the pseudovacuum,\n   here P_1 is a genuine degree-1 polynomial (not the constant 1) and M_k - M_1 = 2 for k=3,4,\n   so under the old monic normalisation those branches really did diverge. This is the state\n   that actually exercises the q_k(u0)=1 change. *)\nord1D = Order1[3, 1, {3, 3, 1, 1}];\nKeyDrop[ord1D, \"sol\"]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
