    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<span style=\"display:none\"></span>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all \"solve\" variables.",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      },
      {
       "data": "{\n\t\"name\": \"WolframKernelMessage\",\n\t\"message\": \"Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all \\\"solve\\\" variables.\",\n\t\"stack\": \"\"\n}",
       "mime": "application/vnd.code.notebook.error"
      }
     ],
     "id": "d2804e5d-674c-48e6-9913-0fb1286d9c8f"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 8.3 Second order\n\nOrder `eps^1` left eight parameters free: the six order-1 rotations and `tc[1]^(1)`, `tc[2]^(1)`. They must be fixed by the order-`eps^2` solvability condition.\n\nUnlike order 1, this step cannot be expected to be linear: the order-2 residual contains `tc^(1) q^(1)`, and both factors carry order-1 free parameters, so the solvability condition is genuinely **quadratic** in them. That is the secular equation of degenerate perturbation theory, not a setup artifact — the check below reports the actual degree rather than assuming either way.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Order eps^2. Fix order 0, substitute the general order-1 solution (its free parameters f1\n   kept symbolic), and inspect the order-2 system before solving it.\n   Total degree in a SET of variables is measured by scaling them all by one marker (Exponent\n   against a list threads componentwise, which is not what is wanted here). *)\nClearAll[Order2, totDeg];\ntotDeg[exprs_, vars_] := Module[{scal}, Max[Exponent[Expand[exprs /. Thread[vars -> scal vars]], scal]]];\n\nOrder2[SS_, PP_, μ_] := Module[{st, Mh, P1, q0, lead0, u1, u2, e1, sol1, f1, sub01, e2},\n   st = PertSetup[SS, PP, μ, 2];\n   Mh = st[\"Mh\"];\n   P1 = QsolveU[μ, SS, PP] /. th; P1 = P1[[1]];\n   q0 = Together[P1/qpoly[P1, u0]];\n   lead0 = Join[\n      Thread[Table[pv[tc[i], 0], {i, 5}] -> (tc0U[μ, SS, PP] /. th)],\n      Flatten[Table[pv[qc[k, j], 0] -> If[j <= Length[q0] - 1, q0[[j + 1]], 0], {k, 4}, {j, Mh[[k]]}]]];\n   u1 = Table[pv[v, 1], {v, st[\"unk\"]}];\n   u2 = Table[pv[v, 2], {v, st[\"unk\"]}];\n   e1 = DeleteCases[Expand[Together[Flatten[st[\"eqs\"][[2]]] /. lead0]], 0];\n   sol1 = First@Solve[Thread[e1 == 0], u1];\n   f1 = Complement[u1, sol1[[All, 1]]];\n   sub01 = Join[lead0, sol1];\n   e2 = DeleteCases[Expand[Together[Flatten[st[\"eqs\"][[3]]] /. sub01]], 0];\n   <|\"f1\" -> f1, \"u2\" -> u2, \"e2\" -> e2, \"sub01\" -> sub01,\n     \"#e2\" -> Length[e2], \"order1 residual\" -> Union[Expand[Together[e1 /. sol1]]],\n     \"degree in f1\" -> totDeg[e2, f1], \"degree in u2\" -> totDeg[e2, u2]|>];\n\nord2vac = Order2[1, 1, {2, 2, 0, 0}];\nKeyDrop[ord2vac, {\"e2\", \"sub01\", \"u2\"}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"vscode-wolfram-message-output\" style=\"color:#f44;border-left:3px solid #f44;background:rgba(255,68,68,0.08);padding:2px 6px;margin:1px 0;border-radius:0 3px 3px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:0.85em;white-space:pre-wrap\">Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all &quot;solve&quot; variables.</div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
