  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* The order-n system leaves free exactly the coefficients along untwisted solutions P_j of\n   degree <= deg Q^(n) -- here qq[n,1] (the P_2 = u direction), plus tcn[1,n], tcn[2,n] as in\n   Section 8. That freedom is NOT gauge: adding a multiple of P_2 lands on a DIFFERENT twisted\n   solution. Fixing it to the known exact values must reproduce Exp[I eps psi_1 u] exactly. *)\ntcExact3 = Module[{x, eqs, tcEps},\n   eqs = Flatten[Table[CoefficientList[Expand[τ[a][1, 1, {2, 2, 0, 0}][x] - τvac[1, 1][a][x]], x], {a, 3}]];\n   tcEps = (tcvars /. First@Solve[Thread[eqs == 0], tcvars]) /. th /. zser[4];\n   Table[Coefficient[Normal[Series[tcEps[[i]], {eps, 0, 3}]], eps, n], {n, 1, 3}, {i, 5}]];\n\nfixRule = Join[\n   Flatten[Table[tcn[i, n] -> tcExact3[[n, i]], {n, 3}, {i, 5}]],\n   {qq[1, 1] -> I psi[[1]], qq[2, 1] -> 0, qq[3, 1] -> 0}];\n\n{\"tc order-1 free directions consistent?\" ->\n   Simplify[(Table[Table[tcn[i, n], {i, 5}], {n, 3}] /. pushSol1 /. fixRule) - tcExact3],\n \"Q^(n) vs exact\" -> Simplify[(recon /. pushSol1 /. fixRule) - Rest[exactPush]]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
