  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 10.3 A maximally split state: `mu = {4,3,1,0}` at `(S,P)=(2,2)`\n\nThe only irrep in the whole `[2,2,0,0] x [2,2,0,0]` decomposition whose four Q-degrees are all distinct: `M = {0,1,3,4}`, `Mhat = {0,2,5,7}`, `dim = 175`. It is also genuinely non-rectangular (`mu1 > mu2 > mu3 > mu4`), and has the widest divergence spread so far — under the old monic normalisation branch 4 would diverge as `eps^-4`.\n\nNo closed form is available here, so validation is by substituting the truncated series back into all four Baxter residuals.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Solve, then validate by residual: substitute the truncated solution back into each branch's\n   Baxter equation and check the eps-expansion vanishes through the determined order. *)\njointX = JointSolve[2, 2, {4, 3, 1, 0}, 6, uu];\n{\"M\" -> jointX[\"M\"], \"q0\" -> jointX[\"q0\"],\n \"#eqs/#unk/#sol\" -> {jointX[\"#eqs\"], jointX[\"#unk\"], jointX[\"#sol\"]},\n \"free\" -> jointX[\"free\"]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"vscode-wolfram-message-output\" style=\"color:#f44;border-left:3px solid #f44;background:rgba(255,68,68,0.08);padding:2px 6px;margin:1px 0;border-radius:0 3px 3px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:0.85em;white-space:pre-wrap\">Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all &quot;solve&quot; variables.</div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all \"solve\" variables.",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
